const resolvedPath = path.resolve(output, urlPath);

if (!resolvedPath.startsWith(resolvedOutput + path.sep) && resolvedPath !== resolvedOutput) {
  res.writeHead(403, ...);
  return;
}
```

This prevents the "similar directory name" attack. `/tmp/ssg-serve-abc` vs `/tmp/ssg-serve-abcdef`: the latter doesn't start with `/tmp/ssg-serve-abc/` (no trailing sep), and it's not equal to `/tmp/ssg-serve-abc`. So 403 fires. Good.

Now let me fix the server code.

